const tvStates=[['Receiver','startup','Starting up'],['Receiver','ready','Ready for your Mac'],['Receiver','offline','No local network'],['Pairing','pairing','Compare six digits'],['Pairing','approval','Remote approval'],['Pairing','declined','Declined'],['Pairing','expired','Pairing expired'],['Sharing','connected','Connection accepted'],['Sharing','live','Live · controls hidden'],['Sharing','controls','Mirroring controls'],['Sharing','paused','Paused on Mac'],['Sharing','lost','Connection lost'],['Sharing','picture','Fit / Fill / Stretch'],['Sharing','margin','Symmetric edge margin'],['Sharing','volume','TV volume guidance'],['Trust & details','details','Viewport / output / ceiling'],['Trust & details','trusted','Trusted Macs'],['Trust & details','forget','Forget confirmation'],['Trust & details','rename','Rename this TV'],['Direct media','media-live','Direct media · controls hidden'],['Direct media','media-controls','Native media controls'],['Direct media','media-paused','Native media paused']];
const params=new URLSearchParams(location.search);
const data={view:params.get('view')||'mac',state:params.get('state')||'ready',theme:params.get('theme')||'light',width:params.get('width')||'420',destination:'Living Room TV',trusted:true,audio:true,route:'both',quality:4,picture:'fit',margin:0,volume:70,source:'Built-in Display',sourceKind:'display',profile:'video',detail:true,follow:true,modal:null,lastState:'ready',lastTrigger:null,forgotten:false,mediaPosition:84,subtitles:'English · external VTT',audioTrack:'English · stereo',file:'Lesson 04.mp4',host:'192.168.1.42',port:'7421'};
Object.assign(data,{tvName:'Living Room TV',tvReturn:'ready',tvForgotten:false,officeForgotten:false,subtitleAttached:false,sourceReturn:'ready',detailsReturn:'live'});
const initialSettings=Object.freeze({...data});
let timers=[];
function later(callback,delay){timers.push(setTimeout(callback,delay));}
function clearTimers(){timers.forEach(clearTimeout);timers=[];}
function announce(text){$('#announcement').textContent=text;}
function go(state,view=data.view){if(view==='mac'){if(state.startsWith('media-'))data.sourceKind='media';else if(data.sourceKind==='media'){data.sourceKind='display';data.source='Built-in Display';}}clearTimers();data.modal=null;data.state=state;data.view=view;render();announce(`${view==='tv'?'TV':'Mac'} prototype: ${state}`);}
function modal(name,trigger){data.modal=name;data.lastTrigger=trigger||null;render();}
function chooseView(view){go(view==='brand'?'identity':view==='icons'?'platforms':view==='system'?'system':'ready',view);}
function header(state='idle',status='Ready',tone='idle'){return `<div class="mac-titlebar"><div class="traffic" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="window-caption">Miraya</span><button class="titlebar-help" data-action="help" aria-label="Connection help">${icon('info','sm')}</button></div><div class="mac-body"><div class="mac-heading">${beam(state,'brand-mark')}<img class="mac-wordmark" src="assets/logos/wordmark-${data.theme==='dark'?'white':'dark'}.svg" alt="Miraya"><span class="status ${tone}">${icon(tone==='error'?'warning':status==='Ready'?'check':'lock','sm')}${status}</span></div>`;}
function footer(content,detail='Encrypted connection',link='Connection help',action='help'){return `</div><div class="mac-footer">${content}<div class="footer-meta"><span class="privacy-note">${icon('lock','sm')}${detail}</span><button class="text-action" data-action="${action}">${link}${icon('chevron','sm')}</button></div></div>`;}
function sourceRows(locked=false,allowSourceChange=false){const direct=data.sourceKind==='media';return `<div class="field-group">${locked?'':`<button class="field-row" data-action="destination" ${locked?'disabled':''}>${icon('display')}<span class="field-copy"><strong>${esc(data.destination)}</strong><small>${data.trusted?'Trusted TV · ':''}Nearby · Illustrative</small></span><span class="row-end">${data.trusted?icon('lock','sm'):''}${icon('chevron','sm')}</span></button>`}<button class="field-row" data-action="sources" ${locked&&!allowSourceChange?'disabled':''}>${icon(direct?'file':data.sourceKind==='window'?'window':data.sourceKind==='area'?'area':'display')}<span class="field-copy"><strong>${direct?'Play original media':esc(data.source)}</strong><small>${direct?'Local file or compatible HTTPS media':data.sourceKind==='display'?'Entire display · 3024 × 1964':data.sourceKind==='window'?'Single window · app audio scope':'Selected area · 640 × 360 points'}</small></span><span class="row-end">${icon('chevron','sm')}</span></button></div>`;}
function preferences(live=false){return `<div class="plain-row"><span class="label">Quality ceiling</span><button class="text-action" data-action="quality">${qualityOptions[data.quality]}${icon('down','sm')}</button></div><div class="plain-row"><span class="label">${icon('speaker','sm')} &nbsp; System audio</span><button class="switch" role="switch" aria-label="Send system audio to TV" aria-checked="${data.audio}" data-action="toggle-audio"></button></div>${`<div class="audio-route"><label for="route">Audio plays on</label><select id="route"><option value="mac" ${data.route==='mac'?'selected':''}>Mac only</option><option value="tv" ${data.route==='tv'?'selected':''}>TV only</option><option value="both" ${data.route==='both'?'selected':''}>Both</option></select></div>${data.route==='tv'?'<p class="hint">Temporarily mutes this Mac’s entire output. Stop or quit restores its previous mute state.</p>':''}`} ${!data.audio?'<p class="hint">TV audio is off. Mac sound uses its current volume and mute.</p>':''}<p class="hint">System audio only. Your microphone is never captured.</p>${live&&data.audio?volumeControl():''}<div class="plain-row"><span class="label">TV picture</span>${live?`<button class="text-action" data-action="picture">${cap(data.picture)}${data.margin?` · ${data.margin}% margin`:''}${icon('down','sm')}</button>`:'<span class="hint" style="margin:0">Available after connection</span>'}</div>`;}
function volumeControl(){return `<div class="volume-row">${icon(data.volume?'speaker':'muted','sm')}<label class="sr-only" for="volume">TV playback volume</label><input id="volume" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="${data.volume}"><output for="volume">${data.volume?data.volume+'%':'Muted'}</output></div>`;}
function cap(text){return text[0].toUpperCase()+text.slice(1);}
function effectivePicture(){return ['738 × 480 · 15 fps','1108 × 720 · 30 fps','1108 × 720 · 30 fps','1662 × 1080 · 30 fps','1662 × 1080 · 30 fps'][data.quality];}
function readyMac(state){const live=['live','paused'].includes(state),paused=state==='paused';let s=header(paused?'paused':live?'connected':'idle',paused?'Paused':live?'Sharing':'Ready',live?'':'idle');s+=`<h1>${paused?'Sharing paused':live?`Sharing to<br>${esc(data.destination)}`:'Share your screen'}</h1><p class="lede">${paused?'The TV may retain its last picture. Resume when you’re ready.':live?(data.audio?'Your selected screen and system audio are being shared.':'Your selected screen is being shared. TV audio is off.'):'Choose a TV and what you want to share.'}</p>${sourceRows(live,paused)}`;if(live)s+=`<div class="delivered"><div><small>${paused?'Last delivered picture':'Sending now'}</small><strong>${effectivePicture()}</strong><small>Selected: ${qualityOptions[data.quality].toLowerCase()}. Output may adapt.</small></div><span class="sample-tag">Illustrative</span></div>`;s+=preferences(live);return s+footer(live?`<div class="footer-actions">${button(icon(paused?'play':'pause')+(paused?'Resume':'Pause'),paused?'resume':'pause',paused?'primary':'')}${button(icon('stop')+'Stop','stop','destructive')}</div>`:button(icon('play')+(data.trusted?'Share to TV':'Pair & share'),'share','primary full'),live?'Local · encrypted':'Pair securely on first use',live?'Connection details':'Connection help',live?'details':'help');}

function errorMac(state){const e=errors[state];return header('error','Needs attention','error')+`<div class="state-symbol error">${icon('warning','lg')}</div><h1>${e.title}</h1><p class="lede">${e.intro}</p>${e.steps.length?`<ol class="list-instructions">${e.steps.map(x=>`<li>${x}</li>`).join('')}</ol>`:''}<details class="error-detail"><summary>Technical details</summary><p>${e.detail}</p></details>`+footer(`${button(e.primary,e.action,'primary full')}${button('Choose another TV','destination','secondary-link')}`,'Nothing is being shared');}
function discoveryMac(state){let offline=state==='offline',empty=state==='no-devices';return header(offline?'offline':'discovering',offline?'Offline':'Finding TVs','idle')+`<div class="state-symbol">${beam(offline?'offline':'discovering',!offline?'beam-motion':'')}</div><h1>${offline?'Living Room TV is offline':empty?'No TV found yet':'Finding your TV'}</h1><p class="lede">${offline?'Its saved pairing is still here. Open Miraya on the TV to reconnect.':'Open Miraya on your TV and leave it ready. TVs appear here on the same local network.'}</p>${!empty&&!offline?'<div class="pair-status"><span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>Looking on your local network…</div>':''}<ol class="list-instructions"><li>Leave Miraya open on the TV.</li><li>Use the same home Wi-Fi or Ethernet network.</li><li>If discovery is blocked, enter the TV’s address.</li></ol><button class="naked-link" data-action="network">Help me find my TV ${icon('chevron','sm')}</button>`+footer(button('Refresh TVs','refresh','primary full'),'No content sent','Enter address','manual');}
function pairingMac(state){if(state==='waiting')return header('discovering','Connecting','idle')+`<h1>Contacting your TV</h1><p class="lede">Your request was received. Waiting for Miraya on the selected TV.</p><div class="pairing-visual">${beam('idle','beam-motion')}</div><div class="pair-status"><span class="spinner"></span>Contacting ${esc(data.destination)}<span class="elapsed">3 s</span></div><p class="hint">Still waiting? You can cancel below. Progress is based on connection milestones, not a made-up percentage.</p>`+footer(button('Cancel connection','ready','full'),'Nothing shared yet');
if(state==='pairing')return header('pairing','Verify TV','idle')+`<h1>Compare with your TV</h1><p class="pair-caption">Make sure these numbers match<br>what you see on ${esc(data.destination)}.</p><div class="mac-digits" aria-label="Comparison code 4 8 1, 7 2 9">481 729</div><div class="pairing-visual">${beam('pairing')}</div><p class="pair-caption">No typing. Compare all six digits.</p><p class="hint" style="text-align:center">Code expires in 1:22 · Illustrative</p>`+footer(`${button('Numbers match','match','primary full')}${button('Cancel','ready','full','style="margin-top:8px"')}${button('The numbers don’t match','mismatch','secondary-link')}`,'Then approve with the TV remote');
if(state==='approval')return header('pairing','Waiting for TV','idle')+`<h1>Approve on your TV</h1><p class="lede">The numbers matched. Now choose <strong>Allow</strong> on the TV using its remote.</p><div class="mac-digits" style="font-size:32px">481 729</div><div class="pairing-visual">${beam('pairing')}</div><div class="pair-status"><span class="spinner"></span>Waiting for TV approval<span class="elapsed">4 s</span></div><p class="hint">Approval expires after 30 seconds. No screen or audio is sent before approval.</p>`+footer(button('Cancel connection','ready','full'),'Nothing shared yet');
const connected=state==='connected';return header('connecting',connected?'TV verified':'Connecting','idle')+`<h1>${connected?'TV connected':'Starting your share'}</h1><p class="lede">${connected?'Your pairing is saved. Waiting for the TV’s first picture.':'Your request was received. You can cancel at any time.'}</p><div class="pairing-visual">${beam('connecting','beam-motion')}</div><ul class="milestones"><li class="done">${icon('check','sm')}Verify the TV’s identity</li><li class="done">${icon('check','sm')}Authorize this Mac</li><li class="${connected?'done':'current'}">${connected?icon('check','sm'):'<span class="spinner"></span>'}Prepare video and system audio</li><li class="${connected?'current':''}">${connected?'<span class="spinner"></span>':icon('display','sm')}Wait for first picture on TV</li></ul><p class="hint">“Sharing” appears only after the TV confirms a presented frame.</p>`+footer(button('Cancel connection','ready','full'),'Local · encrypted');}
function manualMac(invalid){return header('idle','Manual address','idle')+`<h1>Connect by address</h1><p class="lede">Open Connection details on the TV, then enter its address and port.</p><label class="form-field">TV address<input id="host" value="${invalid?'https://192.168.1.42/video':esc(data.host)}" placeholder="192.168.1.42 or living-room.local" ${invalid?'aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="address-error"':''}></label>${invalid?'<p class="inline-error" id="address-error">Enter an IP address or hostname, without a scheme or path.</p>':''}<label class="form-field">Port<input id="port" inputmode="numeric" value="${esc(data.port)}" placeholder="7421"></label><p class="neutral-note">This bypasses discovery, not pairing. You still verify the TV and approve a new Mac.</p>`+footer(`<div class="footer-actions">${button('Cancel','ready')}${button('Connect','manual-connect','primary')}</div>`,'Pinned trust still applies');}
function trustMac(confirm){return header('idle','Saved trust','idle')+`<h1>${confirm?'Forget Living Room TV?':'Trusted TVs'}</h1><p class="lede">${confirm?'This removes its saved permission from this Mac. Pair again to share next time.':'Trust is saved on this Mac. Nearby status comes from current discovery.'}</p>${confirm?`<div class="neutral-note">If this is a different TV than you expected, cancel. Forgetting does not reset the TV itself.</div>`:`<div class="device-list">${!data.forgotten?`<div class="device-option">${icon('display')}<span class="device-name"><strong>Living Room TV</strong><small>Trusted · Nearby · Illustrative</small></span><button class="remove" data-action="forget">Forget…</button></div>`:''}${!data.officeForgotten?`<div class="device-option">${icon('display')}<span class="device-name"><strong>Office TV</strong><small>Trusted · Currently offline · Illustrative</small></span><button class="remove" data-action="forget-office">Forget…</button></div>`:''}</div><p class="hint">Last-seen dates are not stored by the current product. They are deliberately omitted.</p>`}`+footer(confirm?`<div class="footer-actions">${button('Cancel','trusted')}${button('Forget TV','confirm-forget','destructive')}</div>`:button('Done','ready','full'),'Individual trust removal');}
function detailsMac(){return header('connected','Sharing','')+`<div class="connection-label"><h1>Connection details</h1><span class="sample-tag">Illustrative</span></div><p class="lede">Living Room TV · Direct encrypted UDP</p><div class="neutral-note signature-note">No encoder or network limit reported in this sample. Fewer frames can be normal on a static screen or a 24 fps film.</div><h2 class="metric-section">Picture & playback</h2><table class="metric-table"><tbody><tr><th>Requested maximum</th><td>${qualityOptions[data.quality]}</td></tr><tr><th>Actually encoded</th><td>${effectivePicture().split(' · ')[0]}</td></tr><tr><th>TV presentation</th><td>30 fps</td></tr><tr><th>Encoder adaptation</th><td>None reported</td></tr><tr><th>TV frame drops</th><td>2 this session</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="mock-chart" aria-label="Illustrative playback samples, not live data">${[45,47,46,48,45,47,48,47,44,48,47,46,48,47,48,46,48,45,47,48].map(x=>`<i style="height:${x}px"></i>`).join('')}</div><h2 class="metric-section">Local network</h2><table class="metric-table"><tbody><tr><th>Network RTT</th><td>4 ms</td></tr><tr><th>Video jitter</th><td>2 ms</td></tr><tr><th>Recent packet loss</th><td>0.2%</td></tr><tr><th>Video traffic</th><td>6.1 Mbit/s</td></tr><tr><th>Encoder target</th><td>8.0 Mbit/s</td></tr><tr><th>Bandwidth estimate</th><td>9.4 Mbit/s</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 class="metric-section">TV display</h2><table class="metric-table"><tbody><tr><th>App viewport</th><td>1920 × 1080</td></tr><tr><th>Physical output mode</th><td>3840 × 2160 · 60 Hz</td></tr><tr><th>Mirroring ceiling</th><td>Up to 1920 × 1080 · 60 fps</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="hint">RTT is network round-trip, not total display latency. The bandwidth estimate is not a speed test. Router distance and Wi-Fi signal strength are not measured.</p>`+footer(`<div class="footer-actions">${button('Save report…','report')}${button('Done','detail-done','primary')}</div>`,'Measurements · no captured content');}
function mediaMac(state){const playing=state!=='media-ready',paused=state==='media-paused';return header(playing?(paused?'paused':'connected'):'idle',playing?(paused?'Paused':'Playing'):'Ready','idle')+`<h1>${playing?(paused?'Playback paused':'Playing on your TV'):'Play video on TV'}</h1><p class="lede">${playing?'Original media · TV decoder and buffer':'Play original media without sharing your desktop.'}</p>${sourceRows(playing)}${playing?`<div class="media-file">${esc(data.file)} <span class="sample-tag">Illustrative</span></div><p class="hint">1920 × 1080 · original media. Screen-mirroring ceilings do not apply.</p><label class="sr-only" for="seek">Playback position</label><input class="media-seek" id="seek" type="range" min="0" max="720" value="${data.mediaPosition}"><div class="media-timing"><span>${time(data.mediaPosition)}</span><span>12:00</span></div><p class="hint">Buffered ahead: 18 seconds · Illustrative</p><div class="media-controls" style="margin-top:18px"><label>Audio track<select id="audio-track"><option>English · stereo</option><option>Spanish · stereo</option></select></label><label>Subtitles<select id="subtitles"><option ${data.subtitles==='English · external VTT'?'selected':''}>English · external VTT</option><option ${data.subtitles==='Off'?'selected':''}>Off</option></select></label></div>`:`${button(icon('file')+'Choose video or audio…','choose-file','full')}<button class="naked-link" data-action="media-url">Use a direct HTTPS media URL…</button><div class="media-file">${esc(data.file)} <span class="sample-tag">Illustrative</span></div><button class="naked-link" data-action="choose-subtitle">Add SRT / VTT subtitles…</button>${data.subtitleAttached?'<p class="hint">English.vtt · Illustrative <button class="naked-link" data-action="clear-subtitle">Remove</button></p>':''}<p class="hint">Compatible media addresses only. Website pages, login sessions and protected-service licenses are not transferred.</p>`}${volumeControl()}<p class="hint">Audio plays on the TV. For Chrome extensions, choose a screen or window source instead.</p>`+footer(playing?`<div class="footer-actions">${button(icon(paused?'play':'pause')+(paused?'Play':'Pause'),paused?'media-resume':'media-pause',paused?'primary':'')}${button(icon('stop')+'Stop','media-stop','destructive')}</div>`:button(icon('play')+'Play on TV','media-play','primary full'),'Original file via encrypted LAN',playing?'Playback details':'Connection help',playing?'media-details':'help');}
function renderMac(){let state=data.state;let contents=state==='unstable'?readyMac('live').replace('<div class="delivered">','<p class="neutral-note">Picture is adapting. Recent packet loss: 4.2% · Illustrative. Check connection details for the measured limits.</p><div class="delivered">'):errors[state]?errorMac(state):['ready','live','paused'].includes(state)?readyMac(state):['discovering','no-devices','offline'].includes(state)?discoveryMac(state):['waiting','pairing','approval','connecting','connected'].includes(state)?pairingMac(state):state.startsWith('manual')?manualMac(state==='manual-invalid'):['trusted','forget'].includes(state)?trustMac(state==='forget'):state==='details'?detailsMac():state.startsWith('media-')?mediaMac(state):state==='multiple'?readyMac('ready'):state==='reconnecting'?header('connecting','Reconnecting','warn')+`<h1>Reconnecting to your TV</h1><p class="lede">The connection dropped. Retrying only Living Room TV.</p><div class="pairing-visual">${beam('connecting','beam-motion')}</div><div class="pair-status"><span class="spinner"></span>Attempt 2 of 3<span class="elapsed">6 s</span></div><p class="hint">Your screen is not being sent while the connection is down. Cancel stops further attempts.</p>`+footer(button('Cancel reconnect','ready','full'),'Same verified TV only'):readyMac('ready');return `<section class="mac-window ${data.theme==='dark'?'dark':''}" style="--mac-width:${data.width}px" aria-label="Miraya Mac design prototype — ${STATUS}">${contents}${data.modal?renderSheet():''}</section>`;}
function renderSheet(){let title='',body='',actions='';switch(data.modal){
case'destination':title='Choose a TV';body=`<p>Nearby and saved TVs · Illustrative</p><div class="device-list"><button class="device-option" data-action="choose-living">${icon('display')}<span class="device-name"><strong>Living Room TV</strong><small>Nearby · Trusted</small></span>${icon('check','sm')}</button><button class="device-option" data-action="choose-bedroom">${icon('display')}<span class="device-name"><strong>Bedroom TV</strong><small>Nearby · Pair on first use</small></span>${icon('chevron','sm')}</button><button class="device-option" data-action="offline">${icon('display')}<span class="device-name"><strong>Office TV</strong><small>Saved · Currently offline</small></span></button></div><div class="footer-actions">${button('Refresh','refresh')}${button('Enter address…','manual')}</div><button class="naked-link" data-action="trusted">Manage trusted TVs…</button>`;break;
case'sources':title='What would you like to share?';body=`<p>One source at a time. No live preview is used.</p><div class="source-subtitle">Share screen</div><div class="sheet-grid">${button(icon('display')+'Entire display','source-display')}${button(icon('window')+'One window','source-window')}${button(icon('area')+'Selected area','source-area')}</div><div class="source-subtitle">Play original media</div>${button(icon('file')+'Video / audio file or HTTPS media','source-media','full',data.sourceReturn==='paused'?'disabled':'')}${data.sourceReturn==='paused'?'<p class="hint">Stop sharing before switching to direct media.</p>':''}<p class="hint">Use screen sharing for browser-extension overlays. Audio from a window includes its containing app.</p>`;break;
case'quality':title='Picture & playback';body=`<label for="quality-select">Maximum quality</label><select class="quality-select" id="quality-select">${qualityOptions.map((x,i)=>`<option value="${i}" ${i===data.quality?'selected':''}>${x}</option>`).join('')}</select><p>Actual size and frame rate can adapt downward. 60 fps is a maximum, not a promise.</p><hr class="section-divider"><label class="form-field">Profile<select id="profile"><option value="video" ${data.profile==='video'?'selected':''}>Watching video · picture detail</option><option value="desktop" ${data.profile==='desktop'?'selected':''}>Desktop · responsive motion</option></select></label><label class="form-field">Playback priority<select id="priority"><option value="detail" ${data.detail?'selected':''}>Preserve detail · reduce fps first</option><option value="motion" ${!data.detail?'selected':''}>Preserve motion · reduce size first</option></select></label><div class="plain-row"><span class="label">Follow TV resolution</span><button class="switch" role="switch" aria-label="Follow TV resolution" aria-checked="${data.follow}" data-action="follow"></button></div><p class="hint">Uses the TV’s app viewport within this ceiling and keeps the source’s shape. It does not change the Mac’s display mode or enable 4K mirroring.</p>`;actions=button('Done','close-sheet','primary');break;
case'picture':title='TV picture';body=`<p>These change presentation, not encoded quality.</p><div class="picture-choices">${['fit','fill','stretch'].map(x=>`<button class="picture-choice" data-action="picture-${x}" aria-pressed="${data.picture===x}"><img src="assets/ui/picture-${x}.svg" alt="${x==='fit'?'Whole source with bars':x==='fill'?'Edges deliberately cropped':'Source proportions stretched'}">${cap(x)}</button>`).join('')}</div><p>${data.picture==='fit'?'Everything stays visible. Bars may appear. No cropping.':data.picture==='fill'?'Fills the TV by deliberately cropping edges.':'Fills the TV by changing proportions. The image may distort.'}</p><hr class="section-divider"><label class="form-field" for="margin">Edge Margin · <span id="margin-value">${data.margin}% on every edge</span><input id="margin" type="range" min="0" max="10" step="1" value="${data.margin}"></label><p class="hint">One symmetric value compensates for TV overscan. It cannot measure or automatically correct the TV’s physical crop.</p>`;actions=button('Done','close-sheet','primary');break;
case'help':title='Connection help';body=`<p>Open Miraya on the TV and use a network that lets the two devices communicate.</p><ol class="list-instructions"><li>Allow Screen & System Audio Recording when sharing a screen.</li><li>Allow Local Network access if macOS requests it.</li><li>If an enabled screen permission is stale, quit Miraya and refresh only its entry.</li></ol><div class="footer-actions">${button('Check screen access','check-access')}${button('Recording settings…','recording-settings')}</div><button class="naked-link" data-action="network-settings">Local Network settings…</button><p class="hint">Miraya never captures microphone audio. Direct media does not request screen capture.</p><hr class="section-divider"><p>Protected browser video may appear black. The owner confirmed a Chrome graphics-setting workaround on this Mac; behavior varies. There is no Netflix TV-app handoff.</p>`;break;
case'window-list':title='Choose a window';body=`<p>Illustrative window list. In the app this is populated through ScreenCaptureKit.</p><div class="device-list"><button class="device-option" data-action="window-selected">${icon('window')}<span class="device-name"><strong>Chrome — Learning session</strong><small>Only this window is captured</small></span></button><button class="device-option" data-action="window-selected">${icon('window')}<span class="device-name"><strong>Keynote — Presentation</strong><small>Illustrative source</small></span></button></div>${button('Refresh windows','window-list','full')}<p class="hint">Audio is captured at application scope, not isolated to one browser tab.</p>`;break;
case'area-guide':title='Choose an area';body=`<p>The app opens a native overlay on the selected display. Drag a rectangle; press Esc to cancel.</p><div class="neutral-note">This prototype does not inspect your desktop or show a fake preview.</div>${button('Use illustrative 640 × 360 area','area-selected','primary full')}`;break;
case'recording-settings':case'network-settings':title=data.modal==='recording-settings'?'Screen access settings':'Local Network settings';body=`<p><strong>Prototype action.</strong> The app opens System Settings → Privacy & Security → ${data.modal==='recording-settings'?'Screen & System Audio Recording':'Local Network'}.</p><ol class="list-instructions"><li>Find Miraya and enable its access.</li>${data.modal==='recording-settings'?'<li>Quit and reopen Miraya if macOS asks.</li>':''}<li>Return to Miraya and try again.</li></ol><p class="hint">No operating-system setting is changed by this prototype.</p>`;actions=button('Simulate access restored','access-restored','primary');break;
case'check-access':title='Screen access is ready';body='<p>Illustrative successful permission check. This checks capture access only; it does not prove TV reachability or Wi-Fi performance.</p>';actions=button('Done','close-sheet','primary');break;
case'choose-file':title='Choose media';body='<p>Native file selection is represented by an illustrative source, not a fake desktop preview.</p>';actions=button('Use Lesson 04.mp4 · Illustrative','file-selected','primary');break;
case'choose-subtitle':title='External subtitles';body='<p>Choose an SRT or WebVTT file before direct playback starts. The player can then select it alongside supported embedded tracks.</p>';actions=button('Use English.vtt · Illustrative','subtitle-selected','primary');break;
case'media-url':title='Direct media URL';body='<p>A direct HTTPS MP4, HLS or DASH address may work if the TV supports its codecs. A website page or a browser login session is not a media address.</p><label class="form-field">Media address<input id="media-address" type="url" value="https://example.test/lesson.mp4"></label><p class="hint">Illustrative address. No URL is fetched by this prototype.</p>';actions=button('Use illustrative URL','url-selected','primary');break;
case'report':title='Diagnostic report';body='<p>In the app, Save report opens a native save dialog for a local JSON file. Nothing is sent automatically.</p><div class="neutral-note">Up to 72 hours / 2,000 events. Fixed event names and allowlisted numeric measurements only.</div><p>Excludes screen/audio content, file and device names, media URLs, pairing tokens and certificate pins.</p><pre style="font-size:11px;overflow:auto">Illustrative\n{ "event": "sample",\n  "values": { "fps": 30, "rttMs": 4 } }</pre>';actions=button('Done','close-sheet','primary');break;
case'media-details':title='Direct playback details';body='<p>Illustrative · Original media is decoded on the TV.</p><table class="metric-table"><tr><th>Picture</th><td>1920 × 1080</td></tr><tr><th>Buffered ahead</th><td>18 seconds</td></tr><tr><th>Seeking</th><td>Available</td></tr><tr><th>Path</th><td>Original file · pinned TLS</td></tr></table><p class="hint">Buffering can come from source delivery, the network or device decoding. Buffer level alone does not identify the cause.</p>';actions=button('Save report…','report');break;
case'forget-office':title='Forget Office TV?';body='<p>This removes this TV’s saved permission from the Mac. Pair again to share next time. The offline status does not prevent local removal.</p>';actions=`${button('Cancel','close-sheet')}${button('Forget TV','office-forgotten','destructive')}`;break;
default:title='Prototype';body='<p>Illustrative interaction.</p>';}
return `<div class="sheet-backdrop"><section class="sheet" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="sheet-title"><div class="sheet-top"><h2 id="sheet-title">${title}</h2><button class="icon-button" data-action="close-sheet" aria-label="Close dialog">${icon('close','sm')}</button></div>${body}${actions?`<div class="footer-actions">${actions}</div>`:''}</section></div>`;}

function tvHeader(){return `<div class="tv-header"><div class="tv-brand">${beam('connected')}<span>Miraya</span></div><div class="tv-room">${esc(data.tvName)}<small>${data.state==='offline'?'No local network':data.state==='startup'?'Checking local connection':'Local network available'} · Illustrative</small></div></div>`;}
function tvBase(body,cls=''){return `<img class="tv-backdrop" src="assets/backgrounds/tv-beam-lake.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true"><div class="tv-backdrop-scrim"></div><div class="tv-safe tv-scenic ${cls}">${tvHeader()}${body}</div>`;}
function tvFooter(){return `<div class="tv-footer"><div class="tv-actions">${tvButton('Connection details','tv-details','', 'data-default-focus')}${tvButton('Trusted Macs','tv-trusted')}${tvButton('Rename TV','tv-rename')}</div><p class="tv-caption">Keep Miraya open here. On your Mac, choose this TV and Share.</p></div>`;}
function tvLive(state){const media=state.startsWith('media-'),controls=['controls','paused','media-controls','media-paused'].includes(state),paused=state==='paused'||state==='media-paused';let result=`<div class="tv-live-content ${data.picture} ${data.margin?'inset':''}" style="--inset:${data.margin}%"><img src="assets/backgrounds/tv-beam-lake.png" alt="Illustrative shared landscape wallpaper, not an actual screen capture"></div>`;if(paused)result+=`<div class="tv-paused-badge">${beam('paused')}<span>${media?'Playback paused':'Paused on your Mac'}</span></div>`;if(controls){result+=`<div class="tv-control-dim"></div><div class="tv-overlay ${media?'media-controls':'mirror-controls'}"><div class="tv-overlay-heading">${beam(paused?'paused':'connected')}<span>${media?'Original media':'Sharing from your Mac'}</span><span>${data.volume===0?'TV playback muted · ':''}Illustrative</span></div><div class="tv-actions">${media?tvButton(icon(paused?'play':'pause')+(paused?'Play':'Pause'),paused?'tv-media-resume':'tv-media-pause','', 'data-default-focus'):''}${tvButton(icon('display')+cap(data.picture),'tv-picture','',!media?'data-default-focus':'')}${tvButton(icon('speaker')+'TV volume','tv-volume')}${tvButton(icon('info')+'Details','tv-details')}${tvButton(icon('stop')+'Stop','tv-stop','danger')}</div><div class="tv-caption"><span>${media?'Use the remote to control playback.':'Pause / resume mirroring on your Mac.'}</span><span>Back stops ${media?'playback':'sharing'} immediately.</span></div></div>`;}return result;}
function tvPanel(state){let title='',body='';if(state==='details'){title='Connection details';body=`<p>Illustrative measurements</p><div class="tv-property"><span>App viewport</span><strong>1920 × 1080</strong></div><div class="tv-property"><span>TV physical output</span><strong>3840 × 2160 · 60 Hz</strong></div><div class="tv-property"><span>Mirroring ceiling</span><strong>Up to 1920 × 1080<br>60 fps maximum</strong></div><div class="tv-property"><span>Manual connection</span><strong>192.168.1.42<br>Port 7421</strong></div><p class="tv-caption">A 4K output mode does not mean 4K screen sharing. Network RTT is not total display latency.</p>`;}
else if(state==='picture'){title='TV picture';body=`<p>Presentation only. Choose how the source fits.</p>${['fit','fill','stretch'].map(x=>tvButton(`<span class="tv-picture-choice"><img src="assets/ui/picture-${x}.svg" alt=""><span>${cap(x)}<br><small>${x==='fit'?'Whole image · bars may appear':x==='fill'?'Fill TV · crop edges':'Fill TV · change proportions'}</small></span></span>`,'tv-picture-'+x,'',data.picture===x?'data-default-focus aria-pressed="true"':'aria-pressed="false"')).join('')}${tvButton('Edge Margin…','tv-margin')}`;}
else if(state==='margin'){title='Edge Margin';body=`<p>One value adjusts every edge equally.</p><div class="tv-margin"><label for="tv-margin">Margin<span>${data.margin}%</span></label><input id="tv-margin" type="range" min="0" max="10" step="1" value="${data.margin}" aria-label="Symmetric edge margin from zero to ten percent"></div><p>Increase if the TV cuts off corners. It cannot detect physical overscan automatically.</p><p class="tv-caption">Try the TV’s Screen Fit / Just Scan setting too. Fit keeps the whole source visible within the margin.</p>`;}
else if(state==='volume'){title='TV volume';body=`<p>Use your TV remote’s volume and mute keys.</p><div class="tv-note-box">The Mac’s TV playback slider adjusts Miraya’s sound level. It does not change your TV’s master volume.</div><p class="tv-caption">There is no microphone capture. For Mac-only or TV-only output, choose the destination on your Mac.</p>`;}
else if(state==='trusted'){title='Trusted Macs';body=`<p>Remove access for one Mac at a time.</p>${!data.tvForgotten?tvButton('MacBook Pro · Trusted','tv-forget','', 'data-default-focus'):'<p class="tv-caption">MacBook Pro removed. It must pair again.</p>'}<p class="tv-caption">Illustrative device names. Last-seen dates are not stored by the current product.</p>`;}
else{title='Name this TV';body=`<p>The room name appears on nearby Macs. Renaming does not change its saved cryptographic identity.</p>${['Living Room TV','Bedroom TV','Office TV'].map((x,i)=>tvButton(x,'tv-name-'+i,'',!i?'data-default-focus':'')).join('')}<p class="tv-caption">The current receiver also supports custom text using the TV’s native input dialog.</p>`;}
return (data.tvReturn==='ready'?tvBase('<div class="tv-state-main"><h1>Ready for your Mac</h1><p>Receiver settings</p></div>'):tvLive(data.tvReturn==='media-controls'?'media-live':'live'))+`<div class="tv-panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="${title}"><h1>${title}</h1>${body}<div class="tv-actions">${tvButton('Done','tv-panel-done')}</div></div>`;}
function renderTV(){const s=data.state;let content='';if(['live','controls','paused','media-live','media-controls','media-paused'].includes(s))content=tvLive(s);else if(['details','picture','margin','volume','trusted','rename'].includes(s))content=tvPanel(s);else if(s==='forget')content=tvBase('')+`<div class="tv-modal"><div class="tv-modal-card" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="tv-forget-title"><h1 id="tv-forget-title">Forget MacBook Pro?</h1><p>This Mac will need to pair again before sharing. If it is connected now, sharing will stop.</p><div class="tv-actions">${tvButton('Cancel','tv-trusted','', 'data-default-focus')}${tvButton('Forget Mac','tv-forget-confirm','danger')}</div></div></div>`;
else if(['pairing','approval'].includes(s)){const approval=s==='approval';content=tvBase(`<div class="tv-state-main tv-pair"><h1>${approval?'Allow MacBook Pro?':'Compare with your Mac'}</h1><p>${approval?'Only allow this if you are connecting from your Mac now.':'Confirm these six digits match your Mac.'}</p><div class="tv-digits" aria-label="Comparison code 4 8 1, 7 2 9">481 729</div><p>${approval?'Your screen and optional system audio will appear here.':'Choose “Numbers match” on your Mac, then approve here.'}</p><div class="tv-actions">${tvButton(approval?'Decline':'Cancel pairing','tv-decline','', 'data-default-focus')}${approval?tvButton('Allow this Mac','tv-allow'):''}</div><p class="expiry">${approval?'Approval expires in 26 seconds':'Code expires in 1:22'} · Illustrative</p></div>`);}
else if(s==='offline')content=tvBase(`<div class="tv-state-main"><h1>No local network yet</h1><p>Connect the TV to Wi-Fi or Ethernet, then reopen Miraya if needed. Your saved trusted Macs remain here.</p><div class="tv-note-box">Miraya cannot receive while the TV has no reachable local network.</div></div>${beam('offline','tv-beam-small')}<div class="tv-footer"><div class="tv-actions">${tvButton('Refresh connection details','tv-details','', 'data-default-focus')}${tvButton('Trusted Macs','tv-trusted')}</div></div>`,'tv-offline');
else if(s==='startup')content=tvBase(`<div class="tv-state-main"><h1>Getting ready</h1><p>Preparing this TV’s secure identity and local connection.</p><p class="tv-caption">Ready appears only after the receiver starts listening.</p></div>${beam('connecting','tv-beam-small beam-motion')}<div class="tv-footer"><p class="tv-caption">Preparing the local connection…</p></div>`);
else if(s==='lost'||s==='declined'||s==='expired')content=tvBase(`<div class="tv-state-main"><h1>${s==='lost'?'Your Mac disconnected':s==='declined'?'Connection declined':'Pairing expired'}</h1><p>${s==='lost'?'The picture is no longer being received. Check Miraya on your Mac and reconnect when ready.':s==='declined'?'Nothing is being shared. Start a new attempt from the Mac when you want to connect.':'Start again on the Mac and compare a fresh six-digit code.'}</p></div>${beam('error','tv-beam-small')}<div class="tv-footer">${tvButton('Back to ready','tv-ready','', 'data-default-focus')}</div>`);
else if(s==='connected')content=tvBase(`<div class="tv-state-main"><h1>Mac verified</h1><p>Waiting for the first picture from your Mac. A successful connection is not yet a displayed stream.</p></div>${beam('connecting','tv-beam-small')}<div class="tv-footer">${tvButton('Stop','tv-stop','danger')}</div>`);
else content=tvBase(`<div class="tv-state-main"><h1>Ready for your Mac</h1><p>Open Miraya on your Mac.<br>Choose ${esc(data.tvName)}, then Share.</p></div>${beam('idle','tv-beam-small')}${tvFooter()}`);
return `<section class="tv-wrap"><div class="tv-frame ${['details','picture','margin','volume','trusted','rename','forget'].includes(s)?'has-panel':''}" data-tv-state="${s}" tabindex="0" aria-label="Miraya TV prototype — ${STATUS}"><div class="tv-content">${content}</div></div></section>`;}
function palette(){return `<div class="swatches">${[['Deep Navy','#0B1323'],['Near Black','#080F1D'],['Beam Amber','#FF9651'],['Seam White','#FFFFFF'],['Beam Blue','#3478F6']].map(([n,c])=>`<div class="swatch"><div class="color" style="background:${c}"></div><strong>${n}</strong><small>${c}</small></div>`).join('')}</div>`;}
function renderBrand(){return `<article class="board"><p class="board-eyebrow">Miraya — Beam / Identity system</p><h1>Two endpoints.<br>One shared moment.</h1><div class="brand-hero"><img class="hero-logo" src="assets/logos/logo-horizontal-white.svg" alt="Miraya Beam horizontal logo"><div class="hero-copy"><b>A warm source. A cool destination.</b><br>The narrow seam is the connection: separated when idle, aligned for verification, stable while sharing.</div></div>${palette()}<div class="board-grid"><section class="board-tile light"><h2>Light background</h2><img class="logo-sample" src="assets/logos/logo-horizontal-dark.svg" alt="Miraya colored logo for light backgrounds"><p>Neutral interfaces keep the Beam meaningful. Color belongs to the identity and connection moments.</p></section><section class="board-tile"><h2>Dark background</h2><img class="logo-sample" src="assets/logos/logo-horizontal-white.svg" alt="Miraya colored logo for dark backgrounds"><p>Restrained inward light. Concentrated light at the seam. No grain or endlessly glowing controls.</p></section><section class="board-tile light"><h2>Single-color dark</h2><img class="logo-sample" src="assets/logos/beam-mono-dark.svg" alt="Dark monochrome Beam"><p>Silhouette and seam remain recognizable without orange or blue.</p></section><section class="board-tile"><h2>Single-color white</h2><img class="logo-sample" src="assets/logos/beam-mono-white.svg" alt="White monochrome Beam"><p>The bridge is part of the geometry. Glow is never essential information.</p></section></div><section class="board-section"><h2>Beam as a state language</h2><div class="beam-states">${[['idle','Open planes'],['discovering','Brief light activity'],['pairing','Aligned for comparison'],['connecting','Seam brightens'],['connected','Stable seam'],['paused','Narrow, dim seam'],['error','Connection separates'],['offline','Illumination removed']].map(([s,d])=>`<div class="beam-state">${beam(s)}<strong>${cap(s)}</strong><small>${d}</small></div>`).join('')}</div><p class="design-callout">The status is always named in text. The mark supports the message; color and animation never carry it alone.</p></section><section class="board-section"><h2>Material study → reproducible identity</h2><p class="board-lede">The generated study informed light direction and depth. The logo and state marks use editable SVG geometry. Finished app tiles use high-resolution light artwork, with optical vector variants at 16–32 px. This early study informed the material; it is not the final icon master.</p><details style="margin-top:18px"><summary>Inspect the material exploration</summary><img class="study-image" src="studies/beam-material-study.png" alt="Generated Beam material studies — proposal only"></details></section><section class="board-section"><h2>Wordmark, outlined</h2><div class="board-grid"><div class="board-tile light"><img class="logo-sample" src="assets/logos/wordmark-dark.svg" alt="Outlined Miraya wordmark"><p>Optical spacing at a 120-unit source size. Every delivered wordmark consists of paths, with no font dependency.</p></div><div class="board-tile"><img class="logo-sample" src="assets/logos/logo-vertical-white.svg" alt="Vertical Miraya lockup"><p>Vertical lockup for presentation and larger brand contexts. The horizontal lockup leads in product UI.</p></div></div></section><p class="board-eyebrow">${STATUS}</p></article>`;}
function renderIcons(){if(data.state==='small')return `<article class="board small-icon-stage"><p class="board-eyebrow">${STATUS}</p><h1>Beam / actual-pixel-size test</h1><p class="board-lede">Each PNG is displayed at its exact intrinsic size. The 16 and 32 px assets use an optical micro master, not a blurred reduction.</p>${[1024,512,256,128,64,32,16].map(n=>`<div class="size-test-row"><div class="size-meta">${n} px<small>${n<=32?'Pixel-hinted seam. No glow.':'Finished optical material.'}</small></div><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-${n}.png" width="${n}" height="${n}" alt="Beam icon at exactly ${n} pixels"></div>`).join('')}<p class="board-eyebrow" style="margin-top:24px">${STATUS}</p></article>`;
return `<article class="board"><p class="board-eyebrow">One geometry / platform-specific construction</p><h1>An identity you can find.</h1><p class="board-lede">The same opposing planes and central seam, with depth and masks chosen for each platform. Future iOS is a proposal, not an existing app.</p><div class="icon-platforms"><section class="icon-platform"><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-1024.png" alt="Miraya macOS app icon"><h2>Miraya · Sender</h2><p>macOS · Warm source plane emphasized. Inset rounded tile. Restrained rim and inward warm/cool light. Transparent outer canvas.</p></section><section class="icon-platform"><img src="assets/icons/android-tv/icon-1024.png" alt="Miraya Android TV app icon"><h2>Miraya Receiver</h2><p>Android / Google TV · Cool destination plane emphasized. Slightly squarer charcoal-navy tile and a quieter rim. Separate adaptive foreground/background supplied.</p></section><section class="icon-platform ios"><img src="assets/icons/ios-future/icon-1024.png" alt="Future proposed iOS icon"><h2>Future iOS · Sender</h2><p>PROPOSED / FUTURE. Light optical balance. Presentation artwork only. An unmasked vector source is also supplied for future platform adaptation.</p></section></div><section class="board-section"><h2>Sender ↔ Receiver. Related, distinguishable.</h2><p class="board-lede">One Beam silhouette, two endpoint roles. The sender emphasizes its warm source plane; the receiver emphasizes its cool destination plane. At 16–32 px, solid versus outlined planes add a shape cue so color is not the only distinction.</p><div class="role-proof"><div><h3>Sender</h3><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-64.png" width="64" height="64" alt="Sender icon 64 pixels"><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-32.png" width="32" height="32" alt="Sender icon 32 pixels"><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-16.png" width="16" height="16" alt="Sender icon 16 pixels"><p>Source plane solid. Destination plane outlined at micro size.</p></div><div><h3>Receiver</h3><img src="assets/icons/android-tv/icon-64.png" width="64" height="64" alt="Receiver icon 64 pixels"><img src="assets/icons/android-tv/icon-32.png" width="32" height="32" alt="Receiver icon 32 pixels"><img src="assets/icons/android-tv/icon-16.png" width="16" height="16" alt="Receiver icon 16 pixels"><p>Destination plane solid. Source plane outlined at micro size.</p></div></div><div class="micro-zoom"><figure><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-16.png" width="128" height="128" alt="Sender 16 pixel icon enlarged eight times"><figcaption>Sender · 16 px at 8×</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="assets/icons/android-tv/icon-16.png" width="128" height="128" alt="Receiver 16 pixel icon enlarged eight times"><figcaption>Receiver · 16 px at 8×</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="board-section"><h2>TV launcher / 16:9</h2><img src="assets/icons/android-tv/launcher-banner-1920.png" alt="Miraya proposed Android TV launcher banner" style="width:100%;border:1px solid #34445F;border-radius:8px"><p class="board-lede">The symbol and name remain legible across the room. Supplied at 1920 × 1080 and Android TV’s 320 × 180 launcher size.</p></section><section class="board-section"><h2>Small-size optical masters</h2><div class="size-ribbon">${[256,128,64,32,16].map(n=>`<figure><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-${n}.png" width="${n}" height="${n}" alt="Beam ${n} pixel test"><figcaption>${n} px</figcaption></figure>`).join('')}</div><div class="micro-row"><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-16.png" width="16" height="16" alt="16 pixel Beam"><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-32.png" width="32" height="32" alt="32 pixel Beam"><span class="micro-meta">A defined one-pixel white seam.<br>Warm and cool planes remain separate.</span></div><div class="micro-row light" style="margin-top:12px"><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-16.png" width="16" height="16" alt="16 pixel Beam on light background"><img src="assets/icons/macos/icon-32.png" width="32" height="32" alt="32 pixel Beam on light background"><span class="micro-meta">Tested on both light and dark surroundings.<br>No glow, shadow or texture at micro size.</span></div><button class="tv-button" style="font-size:14px;min-height:40px;margin-top:20px" data-action="small-icons">Open all seven actual-size tests →</button></section><p class="board-eyebrow" style="margin-top:30px">${STATUS}</p></article>`;}
function renderSystem(){return `<article class="board"><p class="board-eyebrow">Native controls / shared visual grammar</p><h1>Quiet by default.<br>Clear when it matters.</h1><p class="board-lede">A single compact Mac window and a distant-viewing TV receiver. Connection symbolism is shared; layout and control behavior are platform-specific.</p>${palette()}<div class="board-grid"><section class="board-tile light"><h2>Mac / light</h2><p>System typography. 24 pt content inset, 8 pt spacing rhythm, unified field groups, contextual sheets and a fixed action footer. No main-app sidebar, dashboard or permanent tab bar.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;margin-top:22px"><span class="button primary">Share to TV</span><span class="button destructive">Stop</span></div></section><section class="board-tile"><h2>TV / dark</h2><p>96 × 54 px minimum safe inset at 1920 × 1080. Strong focus, 32 px primary control labels and pairing digits approximately 156 px tall. No persistent chrome during live content.</p><div class="tv-button focused" style="font-size:16px;min-height:48px;margin-top:20px">Focused control</div></section></div><section class="board-section"><h2>Semantic tokens</h2><table class="tokens-table"><thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Mac light</th><th>Mac dark / TV</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody>${[['Background','#F6F7F9','#17202E / #0B1323','Neutral canvas'],['Surface','#FFFFFF','#202C3D / #172237','Groups, sheets, overlays'],['Primary text','#182233','#F4F7FB','Headings and controls'],['Secondary text','#596474','#B4C0D1 / #A8B8CD','Help and measurements'],['Action / focus','#155DDD','#82B1FF / #BCD6FF','Selection, primary action, focus'],['Success','#237348','#86D5A7','Named connected state'],['Warning','#8D4D00','#FFBD75','Recovery guidance'],['Destructive','#BE2C3C','#FF9CA5 / #A92536','Explicit stop / removal'],['Beam only','#FF9651 / #3478F6','#FFFFFF seam','Identity and connection moments']].map(r=>`<tr>${r.map((v,i)=>`<${i?'td':'th'}>${v}</${i?'td':'th'}>`).join('')}</tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></section><section class="board-section"><h2>UI icon usage</h2><p class="board-lede">Use SF Symbols on macOS and Material / native player controls on Android TV. These portable SVGs specify weight and meaning for the prototype; custom picture thumbnails use Beam geometry.</p><div class="system-icons" style="margin-top:22px">${['display','window','area','speaker','muted','lock','shield','refresh','pause','play','stop','info','warning','metrics','file','link'].map(x=>`<div>${icon(x)}<span>${x}</span></div>`).join('')}</div></section><section class="board-section"><h2>Picture modes, deliberately different</h2><div class="board-grid">${[['fit','Whole source, with bars if needed. No crop.'],['fill','Fills the TV by deliberately cropping edges.'],['stretch','Fills the TV by changing proportions; may distort.']].map(([m,t])=>`<section class="board-tile"><img src="assets/ui/picture-${m}.svg" width="160" height="100" alt="${m} illustration"><h2>${cap(m)}</h2><p>${t}</p></section>`).join('')}</div></section><section class="board-section"><h2>Accessibility and motion</h2><p class="board-lede">State names accompany color. TV focus is a high-contrast surface plus a visible ring. Arrow keys navigate spatially; Tab works in the Mac prototype. Dialogs contain focus. Esc closes Mac sheets; Back stops TV playback. Reduced motion disables all pulse, spin and transition effects.</p><p class="design-callout">Beam changes use 160–240 ms opacity/position transitions in the implementation specification. Discovery has only three slow cycles; connected and paused states are static. Stop never waits for animation.</p></section><p class="board-eyebrow">${STATUS}</p></article>`;}
function notes(){let a='',b='';if(data.view==='mac'){a='A native utility, one decision at a time.';b='Destination and source lead. Quality, audio and picture controls are contextual; metrics stay secondary. Every device, code, media item and measurement in this prototype is illustrative.';if(['pairing','approval','waiting','connected'].includes(data.state)){a='Verification is not typing.';b='The numbers are independently derived by Mac and TV. Compare all six digits, confirm on Mac, then explicitly Allow using the TV remote. Sharing waits for the first presented frame.';}if(errors[data.state]){a='Recovery follows the evidence.';b='The message names the observed failure and gives a next action. Network isolation, TV-app closure, permissions and device performance are not guessed from a single symptom.';}}
else if(data.view==='tv'){a='Designed for a remote, not a pointer.';b='Click inside the TV surface, then use arrow keys and Enter. Esc or Backspace represents TV Back: it stops live sharing immediately. Focus starts on Decline for approval and on Cancel for removal.';if(['live','controls','paused'].includes(data.state))b+=' The scenic wallpaper in live previews is illustrative streamed content; a real stream replaces the receiver backdrop completely. Current mirror pause/resume lives on the Mac. TV-side mirror pause would be a future capability; direct-media TV pause is supported.';}
else{a='A reproducible system, not a mood board.';b='Essential assets are standalone SVGs; wordmarks are outlined. Raster platform exports carry proposal metadata. Finished platform icons combine generated optical material with reusable vector masks; logos, optical small marks and interfaces remain reproducible vectors and code.';}
return `<div><span class="eyebrow">Design intent</span><h2>${a}</h2><p>${b}</p></div><div><span class="eyebrow">Product truth</span><h2>Repository behavior wins.</h2><p>No live desktop preview, no microphone, no Netflix handoff and no invented last-seen dates. A 4K panel does not imply 4K mirroring. Quality and frame rates are ceilings; network RTT is not total display latency. <a href="FUNCTIONAL-AUDIT.md">Read the capability audit.</a></p></div>`;}
function statePicker(){const list=data.view==='mac'?macStates:data.view==='tv'?tvStates:data.view==='icons'?[['Icons','platforms','Platform system'],['Icons','small','All seven actual sizes']]:[];$('#state-label').hidden=!list.length;$('#width-label').hidden=data.view!=='mac';$('#theme-label').hidden=data.view!=='mac';const groups=[...new Set(list.map(x=>x[0]))];$('#state-picker').innerHTML=groups.map(g=>`<optgroup label="${g}">${list.filter(x=>x[0]===g).map(x=>`<option value="${x[1]}" ${x[1]===data.state?'selected':''}>${x[2]}</option>`).join('')}</optgroup>`).join('');$('#width-picker').value=data.width;$('#theme-picker').value=data.theme;const advance=$('#advance');advance.hidden=!((data.view==='mac'&&['connected','approval'].includes(data.state))||(data.view==='tv'&&['startup','pairing','connected'].includes(data.state)));advance.textContent=data.view==='mac'&&data.state==='approval'?'Continue approval on TV':data.state==='pairing'?'Simulate Mac confirmation':data.state==='startup'?'Simulate receiver ready':'Simulate first picture';}
let previousModal=null;
function render(){const valid=['mac','tv','brand','icons','system'];if(!valid.includes(data.view))data.view='mac';if(data.view==='mac'&&data.state.startsWith('media-'))data.sourceKind='media';if(data.state==='multiple'&&data.view==='mac'&&!data.modal)data.modal='destination';const focusedId=document.activeElement?.id;statePicker();document.querySelectorAll('[data-view]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-current',b.dataset.view===data.view?'page':'false'));const content=data.view==='mac'?renderMac():data.view==='tv'?renderTV():data.view==='brand'?renderBrand():data.view==='icons'?renderIcons():renderSystem();$('#prototype').innerHTML=`<div class="preview-capture ${data.view}-capture ${data.state==='small'?'actual-sizes':''}" style="--mac-width:${data.width}px">${content}<div class="capture-caption"><span>Miraya / Beam${data.view==='tv'&&['live','controls','paused','media-live','media-controls','media-paused'].includes(data.state)?' · Illustrative shared wallpaper':''}</span><span>${STATUS}</span></div></div>`;$('#state-notes').innerHTML=notes();history.replaceState(null,'',`?view=${data.view}&state=${data.state}&theme=${data.theme}&width=${data.width}`);if(data.view==='tv'){const focus=document.querySelector('.tv-frame [data-default-focus]')||document.querySelector('.tv-frame .tv-button:not(:disabled)')||document.querySelector('.tv-frame');focus?.focus({preventScroll:true});}else if(data.modal){if(previousModal===data.modal&&focusedId&&document.getElementById(focusedId))document.getElementById(focusedId).focus({preventScroll:true});else document.querySelector('.sheet button,.sheet input,.sheet select')?.focus({preventScroll:true});}previousModal=data.modal;}

function time(n){return `${Math.floor(n/60)}:${String(Math.floor(n%60)).padStart(2,'0')}`;}
function closeSheet(){const previous=data.lastTrigger;data.modal=null;render();if(previous)document.querySelector(`[data-action="${CSS.escape(previous)}"]`)?.focus({preventScroll:true});}
function action(a){if(a.startsWith('tv-')){const x=a.slice(3);if(['details','picture','margin','volume','trusted','rename'].includes(x)&&!['details','picture','margin','volume','trusted','rename','forget'].includes(data.state))data.tvReturn=['live','controls','paused','media-live','media-controls','media-paused'].includes(data.state)?(['media-live','media-controls','media-paused'].includes(data.state)?'media-controls':'controls'):'ready';if(x==='panel-done'){go(data.tvReturn,'tv');return;}if(x==='stop'){go('ready','tv');return;}if(x==='allow'){data.trusted=true;go('connected','tv');return;}if(x==='decline'){go('declined','tv');return;}if(x==='mac-match'){go('approval','tv');return;}if(x==='first-frame'){go('live','tv');return;}if(x==='media-pause'){go('media-paused','tv');return;}if(x==='media-resume'){go('media-controls','tv');return;}if(x==='forget-confirm'){data.tvForgotten=true;go('trusted','tv');announce('Illustrative Mac pairing removed.');return;}if(x.startsWith('name-')){data.tvName=['Living Room TV','Bedroom TV','Office TV'][Number(x.slice(5))];data.destination=data.tvName;go('ready','tv');announce('Illustrative TV name selected.');return;}if(x.startsWith('picture-')){data.picture=x.slice(8);render();return;}go(x==='ready'?'ready':x,'tv');return;}
if(a==='sources')data.sourceReturn=data.state==='paused'?'paused':'ready';if(a==='details')data.detailsReturn=data.state==='paused'?'paused':'live';if(['destination','sources','quality','picture','help','window-list','area-guide','recording-settings','network-settings','check-access','choose-file','choose-subtitle','media-url','report','media-details','forget-office'].includes(a)){modal(a,a);return;}
if(a.startsWith('picture-')){data.picture=a.slice(8);render();return;}
switch(a){case'close-sheet':closeSheet();break;case'choose-living':data.destination='Living Room TV';data.trusted=true;go('ready');break;case'choose-bedroom':data.destination='Bedroom TV';data.trusted=false;go('ready');break;case'refresh':go('discovering');later(()=>go('ready'),900);break;case'share':data.lastState='ready';go('waiting');later(()=>go(data.trusted?'connected':'pairing'),650);break;case'new-pair':data.trusted=false;go('waiting');later(()=>go('pairing'),650);break;case'match':go('approval');break;case'continue-tv':go('approval','tv');break;case'first-frame':data.trusted=true;go('live');break;case'pause':go('paused');break;case'resume':go('live');break;case'stop':go('ready');announce('Sharing stopped.');break;case'toggle-audio':data.audio=!data.audio;data.route=data.audio?'both':'mac';render();break;case'follow':data.follow=!data.follow;render();break;case'audio-fallback':data.audio=false;data.route='mac';go('ready');break;case'lower-quality':data.quality=3;go('ready');break;case'access-restored':go('ready');announce('Illustrative access restored.');break;case'confirm-forget':data.trusted=false;data.forgotten=true;go('trusted');break;case'office-forgotten':data.officeForgotten=true;closeSheet();announce('Illustrative Office TV pairing removed.');break;case'manual-connect':{const h=$('#host').value.trim(),p=Number($('#port').value);if(!h||/[\s/]/.test(h)||!Number.isInteger(p)||p<1||p>65535){go('manual-invalid');$('#host')?.focus();}else{data.host=h;data.port=String(p);data.destination=h;data.trusted=false;go('waiting');later(()=>go('pairing'),650);}break;}case'source-display':data.source='Built-in Display';data.sourceKind='display';closeSheet();break;case'source-window':modal('window-list','sources');break;case'window-selected':data.source='Chrome — Learning session';data.sourceKind='window';go(data.sourceReturn==='paused'?'paused':'ready');break;case'source-area':modal('area-guide','sources');break;case'area-selected':data.source='Selected area';data.sourceKind='area';go(data.sourceReturn==='paused'?'paused':'ready');break;case'source-media':data.sourceKind='media';go('media-ready');break;case'url-selected':data.sourceKind='media';data.file='HTTPS video · example.test';go('media-ready');break;case'clear-subtitle':data.subtitleAttached=false;render();break;case'detail-done':go(data.detailsReturn);break;case'file-selected':data.sourceKind='media';data.file='Lesson 04.mp4';go('media-ready');break;case'subtitle-selected':data.subtitles='English · external VTT';data.subtitleAttached=true;closeSheet();announce('Illustrative external subtitles selected.');break;case'media-play':go('media-live');break;case'media-pause':go('media-paused');break;case'media-resume':go('media-live');break;case'media-stop':go('media-ready');break;case'small-icons':go('small','icons');break;case'noop':break;default:go(a);}}
document.addEventListener('click',event=>{const v=event.target.closest('[data-view]');if(v){chooseView(v.dataset.view);return;}const b=event.target.closest('[data-action]');if(b&&!b.disabled)action(b.dataset.action);});
document.addEventListener('change',event=>{const el=event.target;switch(el.id){case'state-picker':go(el.value);break;case'width-picker':data.width=el.value;render();break;case'theme-picker':data.theme=el.value;render();break;case'route':data.route=el.value;data.audio=data.route!=='mac';render();break;case'quality-select':data.quality=Number(el.value);break;case'profile':data.profile=el.value;data.quality=data.profile==='desktop'?4:3;data.detail=data.profile!=='desktop';render();break;case'priority':data.detail=el.value==='detail';break;case'audio-track':data.audioTrack=el.value;announce('Illustrative audio track changed.');break;case'subtitles':data.subtitles=el.value;announce('Illustrative subtitle selection changed.');break;case'tv-margin':data.margin=Number(el.value);render();$('#tv-margin')?.focus();break;}});
document.addEventListener('input',event=>{const el=event.target;if(el.id==='volume'){data.volume=Number(el.value);el.nextElementSibling.textContent=data.volume?data.volume+'%':'Muted';el.setAttribute('aria-valuetext',data.volume?data.volume+' percent':'Muted');}if(el.id==='margin'){data.margin=Number(el.value);$('#margin-value').textContent=`${data.margin}% on every edge`;}if(el.id==='seek'){data.mediaPosition=Number(el.value);document.querySelector('.media-timing span').textContent=time(data.mediaPosition);}});
document.addEventListener('focusin',event=>{document.querySelectorAll('.tv-button.focused').forEach(x=>x.classList.remove('focused'));if(event.target.matches('.tv-button'))event.target.classList.add('focused');});
document.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(data.view==='tv'&&event.target.closest('.tv-frame')){if(['Escape','Backspace'].includes(event.key)){event.preventDefault();if(data.state==='forget')go('trusted','tv');else if(['details','picture','margin','volume','trusted','rename'].includes(data.state))go(data.tvReturn,'tv');else if(['approval','pairing'].includes(data.state))go('declined','tv');else if(data.state==='ready')announce('TV Back would close Miraya and stop discovery. This prototype stays open.');else go('ready','tv');return;}if(['ArrowUp','ArrowDown','ArrowLeft','ArrowRight','Enter'].includes(event.key)){if(event.target.matches('input[type="range"]'))return;if(['live','media-live'].includes(data.state)){event.preventDefault();go(data.state==='live'?'controls':'media-controls','tv');return;}if(event.key==='Enter')return;const focusRoot=document.querySelector('.tv-frame [aria-modal="true"]')||document.querySelector('.tv-frame');const all=[...focusRoot.querySelectorAll('button:not(:disabled),input')].filter(x=>x.getClientRects().length);const current=document.activeElement;const r=current.getBoundingClientRect();const cx=r.left+r.width/2,cy=r.top+r.height/2;const horizontal=['ArrowLeft','ArrowRight'].includes(event.key),sign=['ArrowRight','ArrowDown'].includes(event.key)?1:-1;const candidates=all.filter(x=>x!==current).map(x=>{const q=x.getBoundingClientRect(),dx=q.left+q.width/2-cx,dy=q.top+q.height/2-cy;return {x,primary:(horizontal?dx:dy)*sign,other:Math.abs(horizontal?dy:dx)};}).filter(x=>x.primary>2).sort((a,b)=>(a.primary+a.other*2)-(b.primary+b.other*2));if(candidates.length){event.preventDefault();candidates[0].x.focus();}return;}}
if(event.key==='Escape'&&data.view==='mac'){if(data.modal){event.preventDefault();closeSheet();}else if(['manual','manual-invalid','pairing','approval','waiting','connected'].includes(data.state)){event.preventDefault();go('ready');}}
if(event.key==='Tab'){const dialog=document.querySelector('[aria-modal="true"]');if(dialog){const focusable=[...dialog.querySelectorAll('button:not(:disabled),a[href],input,select,summary')].filter(x=>x.getClientRects().length);const first=focusable[0],last=focusable.at(-1);if(event.shiftKey&&document.activeElement===first){event.preventDefault();last?.focus();}else if(!event.shiftKey&&document.activeElement===last){event.preventDefault();first?.focus();}}}});
$('#advance').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(data.view==='mac'&&data.state==='approval')go('approval','tv');else if(data.view==='tv'&&data.state==='pairing')go('approval','tv');else if(data.view==='tv'&&data.state==='startup')go('ready','tv');else go('live');});
$('#reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{const view=data.view==='tv'?'tv':'mac',theme=data.theme,width=data.width;Object.assign(data,initialSettings,{theme,width});go('ready',view);});
// A deliberately small inspection surface for repeatable local rendering.
window.beamReview={status:STATUS,states:{mac:macStates,tv:tvStates},set:(view,state,options={})=>{Object.assign(data,options);go(state,view);},get:()=>({...data}),render};
render();
